{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more","id":1409094,"title":"Entire Map of The Planes (Mage, Wraith, Demon, Changeling, and more)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-19T02:00:39-07:00","id":1409094,"title":"Entire Map of The Planes (Mage, Wraith, Demon, Changeling, and more)","content":"Hello Everyone! I have drawn 10 drafts in the last week, read about 4 books and still have more to do. I need to make this map and include as much as I can, but between the terminology for each edition Im just a bit confused. Also the more I read of Demon The Fallen the more I love. Just putting that out there. Im starting a Mage 20 group and that question I dread so much comes. &quot;Well what all is in the spirit world?&quot; I plan to tell it, but just for my own sanity during quarantine this will keep me busy between calls. Add as much as you want, rip my understanding to a hole, tear it down and help me get it. I just need help. This is whats getting me through so thank you. TLDR I have trouble with ideas outside reality despite being a witch. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Earth:<br /> <br /> The Gauntlet:<br /> <br /> The Penumbra: As far as I understand, you step from the earth to the penumbra where it reflects the earth, or die and go past the shroud, or astral project to the high umbra.<br /> <br /> <br /> The High Umbra<ul><li>(Highest) Ephemeries: Raw Concepts in symbols, shapes, down to its most basic form</li> <li>(Middle) Spires: Abstract concepts,</li> <li>(Lower) Vulgate: Fully formed concepts, divided by Epiph, where each concept is fully its own mini realm</li> <li>Courts: Where each angel, demon, thoughtform, etc, has its own court reflecting it where they rule.</li> </ul><br /> The Middle Umbra<ul><li>Homelands<ul><li>Black Furies</li> <li>Bone Gnawers</li> <li>Children of Gaia</li> <li>Fianna</li> <li>Get of Fenris</li> <li>Glass Walkers</li> <li>Red Talons</li> <li>Silver Fangs</li> <li>Star gazers</li> <li>Ukenta</li> <li>Wendigo</li> </ul></li> <li>Lost Homelands<ul><li>Black Spiral Dancer / White Howlers</li> <li>Bonyip</li> <li>Croatan</li> <li>Silent Striders</li> </ul></li> <li>Changing Breeds Homelands<ul><li>Corax</li> <li>Nuwisha</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> The Low Umbra<ul><li>The Shroud: Barrier to Death, Called the Agama Sojourn to cross it without dying fully</li> <li>City of the Dead (Wraiths)</li> <li>Malfeas: Realm of The Wyrm</li> <li>Atrocity Realm<ul><li>The Battlegrounds: Where every battle lives out again and again, and you can visit as long as you dont step off the road, or get sucked in until its done.</li> </ul></li> <li>The Tempest (Oblivion, The Abyss?)</li> </ul><br /> Zones: Floating Through The 3 Umbras<ul><li>Mirror Zone</li> <li>Null Zone</li> <li>Ghost Realm</li> <li>Maya (Dream Zone)<ul><li>Chimares: Where each full dream concept has its own pocket</li> </ul></li> <li>Arcadia \u2013 Fae Realm<ul><li>Seelie: Spring and Summer courts</li> <li>Unseelie: Fall and Winter courts</li> </ul></li> <li>Aelder Bole (World/Knowledge/Life Tree)</li> <li>Mount Qaf (Or Olyumpus)</li> <li>Digital Web<ul><li>Spider City<ul><li>Oldtown</li> <li>Uptown</li> <li>Downtown</li> <li>The Pit</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> <li>The Hollow Earth</li> <li>Wolfhome</li> <li>Summercountry</li> <li>Legendary Realm</li> <li>Flux Realm (The Coil: Incarna of The Flux Realm)<ul><li>Entrance: Cocoon</li> </ul></li> <li>Paradox Realms<ul><li>Correspondence</li> <li>Entropy</li> <li>Forces</li> <li>Life</li> <li>Matter</li> <li>Mind</li> <li>Prime</li> <li>Spirit</li> <li>Time</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> Horizon 1: The Asteroid Belt \u2013 Where the feral Incarna Rorg hunts<br /> <br /> Shade Realms:<ul><li>Sun: Governed by All Spheres, Ruled by the Incarna .</li> <li>Moon: Governed by , Ruled by the Incarna Prime.</li> <li>Mercury: Governed by Correspondence, Ruled by the Incarna .</li> <li>Venus: Governed by Life, Ruled by the Incarna .</li> <li>Mars: Governed by Forces, Ruled by the Incarna .</li> <li>Jupiter: Governed by Matter, Ruled by the Incarna .</li> <li>Saturn: Governed by Time, Ruled by the Incarna .</li> <li>Neptune: Governed by Mind, Ruled by the Incarna .</li> <li>Uranus: Governed by Spirit, Ruled by the Incarna .</li> <li>Pluto: Governed by Entropy, Ruled by the Incarna .</li> </ul><br /> Shard Realms:<ul><li>Correspondence</li> <li>Entropy</li> <li>Forces</li> <li>Life</li> <li>Matter</li> <li>Mind</li> <li>Prime</li> <li>Spirit</li> <li>Time</li> </ul><br /> True Horizon/True Horizon: Where Horizon Realms are made<ul><li>Lilith Realms: Nephandi Horizon realms? Or past Horizon?</li> </ul><br /> Deep Umbra:<br /> <br /> <br /> Others to express in the map:<ul><li>Airt</li> <li>Hellholes</li> <li>Hell</li> <li>Trods</li> <li>Moonpaths</li> <li>Moon Bridges</li> <li>Caul: Nephandi portal to the Tempest?</li> <li>Shallowing</li> <li>Glens</li> <li>Erebus: Where werewolves can have their sins burned away in molten pools of silver.</li> <li>Paths into the Abyss<ul><li>Iron:</li> <li>Silver:</li> <li>Gold:</li> </ul></li> <li>Genhinnom: The City where humanity stood with Lucifer (Hollow earth now?)</li> <li>Enoch</li> <li>Caern: Werewolf guarded nodes</li> <li>Pangea: Hollow Earth as Well?</li> <li>Old Roads/Paths of The Wyck</li> <li>Anchorheads</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <br /> THINGS I STILL NEED TO INCLUDE<br /> <br /> Any extra planes, areas from Wraith, Changeling, Werewolf, or other.<br /> The Technocrat terminology for each place and how to express this in a drawn form.<br /> Expansion and Description of each part<br /> <br /> (Side note: Also trying to teach myself Demon The Fallen at the same time as Changeling, Wraith, Werewolf)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our world of darkness podcast: <a href=\"http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2143-niza","name":"Niza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T04:40:03-07:00","id":1409110,"title":"","content":"To be honest I want to have a picture map. I know Horizon the Stronghold of Hope and so on have some but it\u2019s difficult to understand<br /> <br /> I wonder if any fan had drawn it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T04:51:38-07:00","id":1409112,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://trow.cc/board/uploads/post-4-1216266998.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://trow.cc/board/uploads/post-4-1216266998.jpg</a><br /> A fan made map about Underworld","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T04:59:57-07:00","id":1409114,"title":"","content":"Note that the Sun, Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars (And their shard realms) are still within the normal Umbral space, as they are still in front of the first Horizon/Asteroid belt.<br /> Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune and Pluto and the according shard realms are past the asteroid belt, and thus in the Deep Umbra and much harder to reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T05:20:56-07:00","id":1409118,"title":"","content":"OMG wow! This is amazing. I disagree with some of the details, but I really like the overall concept.<br /> <br /> I have my own idea of how things fit together, but tbh I have kind of a short attention span and I have trouble concentrating long enough to put it down into a coherent form.<br /> <br /> Also, I had this idea where you could include D&amp;D and World of Darkness in the same universe, with the Umbral Courts being a modified version of the Outer Planes, the Elemental Courts being the Inner Planes and the different D&amp;D worlds being like distant planets hundreds of light years away from the WoD. I would probably never use it cause the two games are way too different but it\u2019s just a cool idea I was playing around with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T09:26:36-07:00","id":1409151,"title":"","content":"Officially, Malfeas, the Battlegrounds, and the Abyss are in the Middle Umbra. Conceptually, you could change that. I wouldn't put Malfeas in the Low Umbra. The Wyrm is more of a living Corruption rather than the decay of death. The Battlegrounds, though... I wouldn't have put it in the Low Umbra as we know it, but it does match the theme of Memory which the Low Umbra is associated with. The Abyss could be in the Low Umbra, but it occupies the same thematic space as something that is already there: the labyrinth. Better to put it in the Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> If you want to know the general makeup of the Low Umbra it is something like this: Much like the other Umbras, it is a transition from the ephemeral mirror of the real world to the nearly undefined formlessness of the outer reaches. Unlike the others, the transition is not gradual. Also unlike the others, the far edge is not the infinite possibility of the Deep Umbra but the nothingness of Oblivion. The Penumbra of the Low Umbra is known as the Shadowlands. Tear through those and you will find yourself in the monstrous storm known as the Tempest. The major cities of the dead are either built up in the Shadowlands reflections of actual cities or built on the occasional islands of stability in the Tempest. The Tempest doesn't really have directions, but at the &quot;bottom&quot; is the Labyrinth; a dark maze of repressed memories. At the bottom of the Labyrinth is the Maw of the Void, aka the entrance to Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T09:29:17-07:00","id":1409153,"title":"","content":"Okay, a good start, but I feel there are some missing information, or possible mistakes. This might be due to you not being able to see some of the books where the information is. Right off the bat then. The pantheistic spirit courts are part of the Spires, as well as representations of the Afterworlds, as of Infinite Tapestry. You left out the Shadow Lords in the Werewolf homelands, most of ich wouldn't allow Mages who are not Kinfolk. Many of the Realms listed are actually the Near Realms in the Middle Umbra, not in the Zones or elsewhere you listed them. Thirteen recognized by Garou, possibly others not fully understood (Abyss, Arcadia Gateway, Aetherial Reaches, Atrocity Realm, Battleground, Cyber-Realm, Erebus, Flux, Legendary Realm, Pangea, Summer Country, Wasteland, Wolfhome. See Umbra for W20 for more info.). The Underworld is way more complex (Shadowlands, the Tempest with Dark Kingdom of various cultures and Far Shores base on religious thought or smaller cultural views, the Labyrinth home to the Malfeans [who have no known connection to Malfeas, home of the Wyrm in the Middle Umbra, possibly moving from the Far Realms to the Near Realms], the Maw of Oblivion) but check Wraith for greater detail. The Dreaming form Changeling is totally different, with Near, Far, and Deep Dreaming regions leading to the lost Arcadia. Only the first two are accessible to Mages. Check Dreams and Nightmares for C:tD for details. Demon was never integrated into Mage Cosmology, so you have to guess how they fit in. Also, don't forget about the Yomi World from Kindred of the East, a sort of overlap of the Middle/Low Umbra controlled by spirit entities that may have once had ties to the High Umbra. Check The 1,000 Hells for them. By all means read Beyond the Barriers: the Book of Worlds for the best bet, then Infinite Tapestry. The former has a partial map of the Mage Cosmology. It also has a list of all the books published to that point that could help out. I've come up with various theories to map out all the possible spirit worlds, and it is still coming out wrong. The best so far is a double or triple axes view with The Well of Souls opposite the Maw of Oblivion, and Arcadia opposite either true Gaia in the Middle Umbra or so unknown/undiscovered realm representing order in the other direction [it cold involve the Digital Web, or a new type of supernatural, I haven't decide yet.]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T09:56:43-07:00","id":1409160,"title":"","content":"What\u2019s the Well of souls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T11:10:42-07:00","id":1409177,"title":"","content":"In theory, Mage has the largest map of planes, but other lines have many assumptions about the Planes, so it is difficult to sum up them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T11:12:52-07:00","id":1409178,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, it's where Avatars go after mages die. It's not a place that you can visit, and largely exists to explain why Avatars in MRev traverse the Umbra in order to find a new host on Earth. If you're not using that metaplot, there is generally little points to The well of souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T12:37:10-07:00","id":1409192,"title":"","content":"It's an Epiphamie, those places at the top of the Astral Umbra, as per BoW (p. 45), and if I remember correctly IT says little chaged here","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T12:52:37-07:00","id":1409194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more?p=1409112#post1409112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://trow.cc/board/uploads/post-4-1216266998.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://trow.cc/board/uploads/post-4-1216266998.jpg</a><br /> A fan made map about Underworld</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats insanely helpful, thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our world of darkness podcast: <a href=\"http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2143-niza","name":"Niza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T12:55:08-07:00","id":1409196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more?p=1409114#post1409114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that the Sun, Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars (And their shard realms) are still within the normal Umbral space, as they are still in front of the first Horizon/Asteroid belt.<br /> Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus, Neptune and Pluto and the according shard realms are past the asteroid belt, and thus in the Deep Umbra and much harder to reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! I will adjust this to reflect this","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our world of darkness podcast: <a href=\"http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2143-niza","name":"Niza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T12:56:21-07:00","id":1409197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more?p=1409118#post1409118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OMG wow! This is amazing. I disagree with some of the details, but I really like the overall concept.<br /> <br /> I have my own idea of how things fit together, but tbh I have kind of a short attention span and I have trouble concentrating long enough to put it down into a coherent form.<br /> <br /> Also, I had this idea where you could include D&amp;D and World of Darkness in the same universe, with the Umbral Courts being a modified version of the Outer Planes, the Elemental Courts being the Inner Planes and the different D&amp;D worlds being like distant planets hundreds of light years away from the WoD. I would probably never use it cause the two games are way too different but it\u2019s just a cool idea I was playing around with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol dont disagree! Help out! Id loooove to hear your thoughts on it as this is cracking me","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our world of darkness podcast: <a href=\"http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2143-niza","name":"Niza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:04:15-07:00","id":1409199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more?p=1409151#post1409151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Officially, Malfeas, the Battlegrounds, and the Abyss are in the Middle Umbra. Conceptually, you could change that. I wouldn't put Malfeas in the Low Umbra. The Wyrm is more of a living Corruption rather than the decay of death. The Battlegrounds, though... I wouldn't have put it in the Low Umbra as we know it, but it does match the theme of Memory which the Low Umbra is associated with. The Abyss could be in the Low Umbra, but it occupies the same thematic space as something that is already there: the labyrinth. Better to put it in the Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> If you want to know the general makeup of the Low Umbra it is something like this: Much like the other Umbras, it is a transition from the ephemeral mirror of the real world to the nearly undefined formlessness of the outer reaches. Unlike the others, the transition is not gradual. Also unlike the others, the far edge is not the infinite possibility of the Deep Umbra but the nothingness of Oblivion. The Penumbra of the Low Umbra is known as the Shadowlands. Tear through those and you will find yourself in the monstrous storm known as the Tempest. The major cities of the dead are either built up in the Shadowlands reflections of actual cities or built on the occasional islands of stability in the Tempest. The Tempest doesn't really have directions, but at the &amp;quot;bottom&amp;quot; is the Labyrinth; a dark maze of repressed memories. At the bottom of the Labyrinth is the Maw of the Void, aka the entrance to Oblivion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you thank you thank you! Slowly its coming together. Can you help me out with Defining The Abyss?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our world of darkness podcast: <a href=\"http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2143-niza","name":"Niza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T13:31:01-07:00","id":1409208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more?p=1409153#post1409153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, a good start, but I feel there are some missing information, or possible mistakes. This might be due to you not being able to see some of the books where the information is. Right off the bat then. The pantheistic spirit courts are part of the Spires, as well as representations of the Afterworlds, as of Infinite Tapestry. You left out the Shadow Lords in the Werewolf homelands, most of ich wouldn't allow Mages who are not Kinfolk. Many of the Realms listed are actually the Near Realms in the Middle Umbra, not in the Zones or elsewhere you listed them. Thirteen recognized by Garou, possibly others not fully understood (Abyss, Arcadia Gateway, Aetherial Reaches, Atrocity Realm, Battleground, Cyber-Realm, Erebus, Flux, Legendary Realm, Pangea, Summer Country, Wasteland, Wolfhome. See Umbra for W20 for more info.). The Underworld is way more complex (Shadowlands, the Tempest with Dark Kingdom of various cultures and Far Shores base on religious thought or smaller cultural views, the Labyrinth home to the Malfeans [who have no known connection to Malfeas, home of the Wyrm in the Middle Umbra, possibly moving from the Far Realms to the Near Realms], the Maw of Oblivion) but check Wraith for greater detail. The Dreaming form Changeling is totally different, with Near, Far, and Deep Dreaming regions leading to the lost Arcadia. Only the first two are accessible to Mages. Check Dreams and Nightmares for C:tD for details. Demon was never integrated into Mage Cosmology, so you have to guess how they fit in. Also, don't forget about the Yomi World from Kindred of the East, a sort of overlap of the Middle/Low Umbra controlled by spirit entities that may have once had ties to the High Umbra. Check The 1,000 Hells for them. By all means read Beyond the Barriers: the Book of Worlds for the best bet, then Infinite Tapestry. The former has a partial map of the Mage Cosmology. It also has a list of all the books published to that point that could help out. I've come up with various theories to map out all the possible spirit worlds, and it is still coming out wrong. The best so far is a double or triple axes view with The Well of Souls opposite the Maw of Oblivion, and Arcadia opposite either true Gaia in the Middle Umbra or so unknown/undiscovered realm representing order in the other direction [it cold involve the Digital Web, or a new type of supernatural, I haven't decide yet.]</div> </div> </div> </div>You have both enlightened and frustrated me and its all I could have asked for. The way I see it, the technocrats (I think) Nuked the elder vamp and cracked the gates to hell. Demon describes hell as this pit where you cant even tell it has layers. Its just a void only marked by you knowing youre in one and causes numbness. The angels talk about how they shaped the universe and I was thinking, either Sky Daddy locked them into a pit in the Low Umbra where the only door was back to earth but not to the other layers of the umbras. Or in the deeeeep umbra, where sky daddy knew humans wouldnt be able to even see them like a star considering the orders of &quot;Dont be seen&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our world of darkness podcast: <a href=\"http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2143-niza","name":"Niza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T15:26:34-07:00","id":1409236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more?p=1409199#post1409199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you thank you thank you! Slowly its coming together. Can you help me out with Defining The Abyss?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mmmm, crossover cosmology.<br /> <br /> So, &quot;the Abyss&quot; is one of the more problematic aspects of crossover cosmology for the Old World of Darkness because it has specific connotations within different game lines that do not (necessarily) match up:<br /> <br /> In Vampire, &quot;the Abyss&quot; was historically treated mostly as a piece of lore and power-source for the Obtenebration Discipline of the Lasombra Clan; while the magical practitioners of Abyss Mysticism had an intensely nihilistic &quot;return to the pre-Creation void&quot; philosophy going on, the cosmology-lite nature of Vampire means it gets relatively little solid fleshing-out. At least until V5 where they have linked it more explicitly with Oblivion IIRC.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf, &quot;the Abyss&quot; is a Near Realm associated with death, destruction, and lost things. While definitely part of the Middle Umbra, it has enough of a connection the the Low Umbra that a bunch of wraiths seem to have found their way there.<br /> <br /> In Demon, &quot;the Abyss&quot; is defined predominantly as a featureless void at the edge or bottom of Creation. It is pure Nothingness, or the edge of it at least. It does seem to be &quot;adjacent&quot; to the Lower Umbra in a cosmological sense, since I recall an account of a Fallen mentioning tormenting the souls of the dead. But depending on who you ask, the reliability of the memories of the Fallen is questionable.<br /> <br /> Where cosmological questions in the World of Darkness get really tricky is that the precise answer to the question of &quot;how are all of these things related&quot; is going to vary greatly depending on what kind of story you want to tell, and which particular &quot;facts&quot; you choose to regard as canon as a result. To use an example, a chronicle that ultimately wishes to affirm an Abrahamic religious worldview is likely going to have a very different cosmology from one which chooses to subvert or deconstruct it. A game that favours Werewolf mythology will probably come up with different answers than a game that favours Demon mythology.<br /> <br /> To go back to the example of the Abyss, I have not entirely settled all of my answers of how I want to handle it in my stories. But I do tend to favour an approach that has them connected to some extent, rather than completely different things which just coincidentally have the same name. Similar to Zones, &quot;the Abyss&quot; is a feature of the Tellurian that crosses the boundaries of the High, Middle, and Low Umbras in my personal canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T15:44:48-07:00","id":1409241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more?p=1409178#post1409178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly, it's where Avatars go after mages die. <i>It's not a place that you can visit</i>,</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaaactually that last part is not quite true. And as I'm writing this, I find more and more ways to reach it, heh. This was actually supposed to be a short quip.<br /> <br /> *inhales*<br /> <br /> The well of souls' entrance actually bears human writings in the long tunnel leading to it, and ancient humans have supposedly been there (Book of worlds pg 45, IT page 100). Infinity Tapestry actually describes Polymnia, the muse of (huh) Religion that can actually help you find it via a Boon (page 75), and page 90 describes how the &quot;Continuum Orrery&quot; Epiphany can be used to reach the Well as..uh...well. Well well.<br /> Another way of reaching it is through the Well of Remembrance (pg. 100), where you have to actually dive deep down into this well to emerge in the Well of Souls Epiphany.<br /> <br /> ...visiting the Well of Souls has interesting effects, to say the least. It's a limitless node (So Nodes can exist away from Earth. HA.). But staying too long makes Mages slowly take on the shape and form of their Avatars. Among other strange things happening overall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T16:06:51-07:00","id":1409245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more#post1409094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]The Shroud: Barrier to Death, Called the Agama Sojourn to cross it without dying fully</div> </div> </div> </div>Also mention that it can be entered physically via certain rotes/paradigms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Malfeas: Realm of The Wyrm[*]Atrocity Realm[*]The Battlegrounds: Where every battle lives out again and again, and you can visit as long as you dont step off the road, or get sucked in until its done. </div> </div> </div>Deep and middle umbras respectively.[/LIST]<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Horizon 1: The Asteroid Belt \u2013 Where the feral Incarna Rorg hunts </div> </div> </div>Rorg and the Aetherial Realm in general are in the Middle Umbra - they might be thought of as more of a &quot;realm of astrology&quot; than a &quot;space realm&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [*]Erebus: Where werewolves can have their sins burned away in molten pools of silver. </div> </div> </div>Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Technocrat terminology for each place and how to express this in a drawn form: </div> </div> </div>High Umbra: Ensemble Space<br /> Middle Umbra: Biospheric Space<br /> Low Umbra: Entropic Space<br /> Etherspace: Subspace<br /> Deep Umbra: Void<br /> First Horizon: Biospheric Horizon<br /> Second Horizon: Anthropic Horizon<br /> (Second Horizon is also called the Barrier)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T18:06:07-07:00","id":1409255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more?p=1409241#post1409241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...visiting the Well of Souls has interesting effects, to say the least. It's a limitless node (So Nodes can exist away from Earth. HA.). But staying too long makes Mages slowly take on the shape and form of their Avatars. Among other strange things happening overall.</div> </div> </div> </div> For what it's worth, I don't think anyone has said that Nodes are unique to Earth; only that Nodes tied to Earth are the only ones you can use without some sort of \u201cstaying too long\u201d effect: in particular, you need ties to Earth-based Nodes to maintain a Voidship's environment. \u201cTurning into the likeness of your Avatar\u201d is one example of what can happen if you don't have access to \u201cEarth-flavored\u201d Quintessence to keep the environment Earth-like. <br /> <br /> That said, I'd personally allow Quintessence from sources anywhere in Conventional Space, not just on Earth, to be \u201csafe\u201d for a Voidship's environment. It's when you try to tap into sources found in Subspace or the Deep Universe that things get weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-19T20:31:13-07:00","id":1409275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Czernobog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1409094-entire-map-of-the-planes-mage-wraith-demon-changeling-and-more?p=1409245#post1409245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also mention that it can be entered physically via certain rotes/paradigms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Deep and middle umbras respectively.[/LIST]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Rorg and the Aetherial Realm in general are in the Middle Umbra - they might be thought of as more of a &quot;realm of astrology&quot; than a &quot;space realm&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> Middle Umbra.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> High Umbra: Ensemble Space<br /> Middle Umbra: Biospheric Space<br /> Low Umbra: Entropic Space<br /> Etherspace: Subspace<br /> Deep Umbra: Void<br /> First Horizon: Biospheric Horizon<br /> Second Horizon: Anthropic Horizon<br /> (Second Horizon is also called the Barrier)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> THANK YOU it helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Our world of darkness podcast: <a href=\"http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://thesundaysix.podbean.com/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2143-niza","name":"Niza","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2143_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T07:37:10-08:00","id":1474805,"title":"","content":"Ever been able to finish that map?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11871-tsalmaveth","name":"Tsalmaveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11871_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T06:12:37-08:00","id":1474843,"title":"","content":"I once came up with a visualization for how you might conceptualize the Dark Umbra. <br /> <br /> Imagine a large soda bottle uncapped, inverted, and filled with a boiling, churning, chunky liquid. Soup is probably safest. The liquid is spiraling out the hole, but the chunks are caught in the tube, clogging it. The soup is the Tempest. The clog is the Labyrinth. The hole is Oblivion. Now take a map of the world and stick it to the inside surface of the bottle. That's the Shadowlands. Take some other smaller maps of fallen cities and imaginary lands and dump them into the soup to swirl around. Those are stable places in the Tempest like Stygia and the Far Shores. Take a bunch of cut outs of roads and rivers and attach them with one end to the Shadowlands and one end to one of the stable islands. They will writhe in the soup, but their endpoints remain attached to the same places. These are Byways.<br /> <br /> It's great for the Dark Umbra, not so good for others. Does anyone have any good visualizations for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-17T15:46:06-08:00","id":1474875,"title":"","content":"Trying to make an actual map of the various Otherworlds would probably require third or even fourth dimensional modeling, If not more given how several of these places inhabit the same area just at different frequencies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T08:47:38-08:00","id":1474903,"title":"","content":"So the planets in space are just physical representations of the planets of the Umbra? I know Space as mortals know it is just the Umbra essentially. You can reach it via a spaceship as the Void Engineers will tell you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-18T09:50:49-08:00","id":1474908,"title":"","content":"The planets in space once were quite different than they are today. They were, as old tales and myths described them, mystic and alien worlds, back in the time when travelling into the umbra literally was doable by jumping into an airship in the Rennaisance and flying up. There was no 'classic space'.<br /> The spread of the Technocracy's reality, combined with the 'formatting' of space by the Void Engineers, essentially pushed the normal, scientific cold concept of space outward - essentially expanding 'normal' reality - and the Umbral representations of those planets got pushed behind the expanding gauntlet, leaving cold dead rocks and gas giants to the observer.<br /> <br /> This area ranges up to our solar system's asteroid belt, which is the 'second horizon' that leads into the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> Now, yes, the planets - at least their true selves beyond the gauntlet, on the Umbral side of things, are the Shard Realms of &lt;insert sphere here&gt;, while the shadow they cast on Earth's gauntlet are the 'Shade Realms of &lt;insert sphere here&gt;'. The Shade Realms are easier to reach due to the closer 'proximity' and also tend to be less...hazardous than the full blown Shard Realms.<br /> <br /> Of note is that there is no SR Prime. Some claim that it's the Sun, but other theories are that SR Prime is actually Earth - and since it was observed that each Shard Realm seems to be a gateway to a whole universe-like representation of that sphere, that our universe is actually the Prime-universe connected to SR Prime (Be it Sol or Earth - each would make sense, giving Sol's energy, and Earth's Prime nodes).<br /> <br /> An if this sounds confusing, welcome to Mage cosmology. It's an awesome ride.<br /> I suggest reading Beyond The Barriers and Infinite Tapestry. Both are really really good books about Mage cosmology, one 2nd, one Revised, each with kind of a different focus on things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-18-2022, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-20T10:12:58-08:00","id":1475047,"title":"","content":"Until M20 gets a Guide to the Otherworlds, this will be very confusing. Anyway, I myself have tried to come up with a thee (or three-and-a-half) dimensional map consisting of seven (!) different sections with six of them having five different contiguous layers in opposing pairs based on three different scales [creation/destruction, physical/spiritual, chaos/order] and multiple zones/pockets that interspersed between them. Not all of the layers currently exist in their original forms, but they are still there in some form. I've mentioned it in other forums/posts. The main problem with it is that Earth/physical reality is just one of those sections and not the center, designated Midgard/Mt. Qaf/etc. It also seems to entail having a previous destroyed reality (Exalted) as a basis, with some of its elements surviving and either helping/interfering in the creation of the current WOD. Also, I have the two of the original sections combined to create a new 'sixth' section and have a new center point formed. Yes, I'm overcomplicating things, but it is a solution that allows crossover of all WOD game lines as well as their histories with as few hiccups as possible. One day, I might even start writing up each individual location and theory as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T11:44:53-08:00","id":1475648,"title":"","content":"I've never really liked the Shard Realms and Shade Realms. They imply that the Spheres are metaphysical elements of the world rather than terminology invented by the Trads and Techies to discuss magic. As important ideas with hundreds of years of history they should have a strong presence in the High Umbra, but the association with major planets shouldn't be as strong as it is.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-01T12:08:01-08:00","id":1475650,"title":"","content":"And then you run into problems like the Shard/Shade Realm of Entropy, i.e., Pluto, now that its status as a planet is, at best, in doubt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-02T09:35:55-08:00","id":1475666,"title":"","content":"Astrophysicists are actually talking abutting bumping Pluto back up to full planet status, along with maybe another minor planet or two. The connections between the Shade and Shard Realms are tenuous as the planets existed long before the Sphere Magic Theory came about. The Shade Realms may have come into being as soon as humans knew about the planet, but the Shard Realms and their connections came about only with the idea of the Spheres. One last piece of trivia, Uranus can be seen with the naked eye, if you really look for it. I believe that some ancient civilizations may have known this and included Uranus in their astronomy/astrology. How this throws the Shard/Shade Realm into chaos is open for debate, or at least of a really good hook for an SV supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T10:17:48-08:00","id":1475738,"title":"","content":"To be clear it's not the idea of the celestial bodies casting a shadow on the earthly umbra that I dislike. That\u2019s a fun idea. <br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t makes sense for those bodies and their shadows having anything to do with the Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 03-11-2022, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}